{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he took.</b> When he read in the ears of the elders and they accepted upon themselves, then he took half of the remaining blood, and they splashed it on the people — and they are the elders, for they stand in place of all Israel, as is written regarding the bull of the congregation's hidden matter: and the elders of the congregation shall lean their hands (Leviticus 4:15) — for they stand in place of all Israel:" "And this splashing is like: and he sprinkled on Aaron, on his garments (Leviticus 8:30)." "And it is called the blood of the covenant."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:56.801162832Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}